# ---- watchdog responder: prefetched evidence (BH-654, hub only) ----
# bin/watchdog-responder.sh fetches each persisted ticket's thread, decision
# fields and open-PR state itself, then spends a no-tools DECISION call on that
# fixed evidence and today's tooled ACT call only when a decision says an act is
# owed. The lane was carrying a median 4.27M input tokens per call because the
# prompt told the model to go and find all of that through the tool loop.
# Comments kept per ticket (bin/board-fetch.sh --last: the first comment plus
# the newest N, with the omission count rendered).
#RESPONDER_THREAD_COMMENTS=10
# Ceiling on the WHOLE rendered prompt, in bytes. The fixed scaffold is measured
# first and the remainder is split evenly across the keys; inside a key comments
# are dropped OLDEST-first, because the newest comment defines the current ask.
# Every drop is named in the prompt. A value below the fixed scaffold cannot be
# honoured: the evidence is dropped and logs/responder.log says so.
#RESPONDER_EVIDENCE_CAP_BYTES=60000
# Hard ceiling on gh calls per pass (one `pr list` per key plus one `pr view`
# per PR found). Past it, and whenever bin/lib/gh-budget.sh says the token is
# low, the prompt says "PR state: MISSING (…)" — never "none open matching",
# which would read as a verified absence.
#RESPONDER_PR_CALLS_MAX=12
# Kill switches: flags/responder-disabled turns the whole lane off;
# flags/responder-prefetch-off restores the single tooled call on today's
# prompt, byte for byte (no prefetch, no decision call, no AGENT_CALL_NO_TOOLS).

